1. DEFINITIONS
============================================================

1.1 "Rawline" means the Rawline operating system and all source code,
kernel code, system components, build files, documentation, interfaces,
configuration, and other materials distributed by the Licensor under
this License.

1.2 "Licensor" means the copyright holder of Rawline, initially
EXOFORCE, and any lawful successor or assignee.

1.3 "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under
this License.

1.4 "Source Code" means the preferred form for making modifications,
including source files, build scripts, dependency information,
configuration, generated interface definitions where necessary,
installation instructions, and other materials reasonably required to
reproduce the relevant binary.

1.5 "Object Code" means compiled, packaged, linked, or otherwise
non-source forms of Rawline.

1.6 "Modified Rawline" means Rawline or any portion of Rawline that has
been modified, extended, adapted, replaced, or combined with code in a
manner that creates a derivative work of Rawline.

1.7 "Rawline Component" means any kernel, kernel module, core system
service, core runtime, system library, or other component distributed
as part of Rawline.

1.8 "Application" means software that runs on Rawline through public,
documented application interfaces, system calls, IPC protocols, command
line interfaces, runtime APIs, or libraries intended by the Licensor
for ordinary application development.

1.9 "Public Driver API" means an interface expressly designated by the
Licensor as a stable interface for third-party drivers.

1.10 "Kernel Module" means code loaded into or linked with the Rawline
kernel address space, regardless of whether dynamically or statically
loaded.

1.11 "Distribute" means making Rawline or Modified Rawline available to
a third party in Source Code or Object Code form, whether separately or
embedded in another product.

1.12 "Commercial Use" means use primarily intended to generate revenue,
commercial advantage, or other direct economic benefit.

1.13 "Rawline Product" means a product or service in which Rawline
itself, a Rawline-derived operating system, Rawline hosting, Rawline
virtual machines, Rawline desktops, or substantially equivalent Rawline
functionality is marketed, licensed, sold, rented, or provided as the
product or a material selling point.

1.14 "Incidental Commercial Use" means commercial use where Rawline is
merely an underlying operating system or infrastructure layer and is
not itself the product being sold or marketed.

Examples include:

(a) developing or selling an Application that runs on Rawline;
(b) operating a website, game server, database, AI service, build
    system, or internal workstation on Rawline;
(c) using Rawline internally within a commercial organization; and
(d) shipping Rawline as an underlying operating system inside a broader
    hardware or software product whose principal product is not Rawline
    itself.

1.15 "Hosted Rawline Service" means a service that provides Rawline
itself to third parties, including hosted Rawline virtual machines,
remote Rawline desktops, managed Rawline installations, Rawline shell
access, or similar offerings.

1.16 "Public Use" means use of Rawline or Modified Rawline by persons
outside Your household or organization, excluding ordinary users of
Applications or services merely running on Rawline.

1.17 "Contribution" means copyrightable material intentionally submitted
to the Licensor for inclusion in Rawline.

1.18 "Contributor" means a person or entity that submits a Contribution.

1.19 "Trademarks" means "Rawline", Rawline logos, EXOFORCE marks, and
other names or marks owned by the Licensor.


============================================================
2. PERSONAL AND INTERNAL USE
============================================================

2.1 You may, without payment:

(a) download and run Rawline;
(b) inspect and study its Source Code;
(c) reproduce it for Your own use;
(d) modify it privately;
(e) create private forks;
(f) use it for education, experimentation, research, development, and
    testing; and
(g) use it internally within an organization, including a commercial
    organization.

2.2 Commercial organizations may use Rawline internally without payment
provided Rawline itself is not being offered as a Rawline Product.

2.3 Private modifications that are not Distributed and are not used to
provide a Hosted Rawline Service may remain private.


============================================================
3. APPLICATIONS AND SOFTWARE RUNNING ON RAWLINE
============================================================

3.1 Applications are not subject to this License merely because they:

(a) run on Rawline;
(b) invoke Rawline system calls;
(c) communicate through documented IPC mechanisms;
(d) use documented command-line interfaces;
(e) use documented network protocols;
(f) link, statically or dynamically, against public Rawline application
    libraries intended for ordinary application development; or
(g) use the Public Driver API where permitted by Section 4.

3.2 Applications may be:

(a) proprietary;
(b) commercial;
(c) free;
(d) open source;
(e) source available; or
(f) licensed under any other terms chosen by their authors.

3.3 Nothing in this License gives the Licensor ownership of software
merely because that software runs on Rawline.

3.4 Commercial software may be developed, sold, licensed, or operated
on Rawline without paying the Licensor merely for using Rawline as an
operating system.


============================================================
4. DRIVERS AND KERNEL MODULES
============================================================

4.1 A driver using only the documented Public Driver API may be
proprietary or licensed under any terms chosen by its author.

4.2 Use of undocumented, private, internal, unstable, or kernel-private
interfaces may cause a work to be considered a Modified Rawline work.

4.3 Every Kernel Module derived from, linked into, or loaded into the
Rawline kernel must be licensed under this License unless the Licensor
has separately authorized different terms.

4.4 The Licensor may design Rawline so that proprietary hardware support
can be implemented in userspace through stable public interfaces.


