============================================================

5.1 You may redistribute unmodified Rawline without separate permission
only if:

(a) the redistribution is non-commercial;
(b) no fee is charged for Rawline itself;
(c) all license and copyright notices are preserved;
(d) the redistribution does not imply endorsement by the Licensor; and
(e) this License accompanies the redistribution.

5.2 Reasonable reimbursement of unavoidable physical media or shipping
costs is permitted only where no profit is made from the redistribution.

5.3 You may redistribute Modified Rawline without separate permission
only if:

(a) the redistribution is non-commercial;
(b) the requirements of Sections 8 through 11 are satisfied; and
(c) the resulting work is licensed under this License.


============================================================
6. COMMERCIAL USE OF RAWLINE ITSELF
============================================================

6.1 You may not, without separate written permission from the Licensor:

(a) sell Rawline;
(b) sell a Modified Rawline operating system;
(c) commercially license Rawline or Modified Rawline;
(d) offer Rawline as a paid operating-system distribution;
(e) commercially distribute a fork whose product is substantially
    Rawline itself;
(f) operate a Hosted Rawline Service; or
(g) otherwise monetize Rawline itself as a Rawline Product.

6.2 Publication of Source Code does not by itself grant permission for
commercial exploitation prohibited by this Section.

6.3 A fully source-available commercial Rawline fork still requires a
separate commercial agreement with the Licensor.

6.4 The Licensor may grant commercial rights under separate terms,
including royalty-bearing, revenue-sharing, flat-fee, OEM, cloud,
enterprise, or other agreements.


============================================================
7. INCIDENTAL COMMERCIAL USE
============================================================

7.1 Incidental Commercial Use is permitted.

7.2 Examples include:

(a) commercial Applications running on Rawline;
(b) commercial game development;
(c) software development workstations;
(d) commercial servers whose service is not Rawline itself;
(e) websites hosted on Rawline;
(f) AI inference or development workloads running on Rawline;
(g) internal business infrastructure; and
(h) hardware products that use Rawline merely as their underlying
    operating system.

7.3 If Rawline is distributed as part of a broader commercial product,
any modifications made to Rawline itself remain subject to the source
obligations of this License.

7.4 This Section does not permit marketing Rawline itself as a product
without authorization under Section 6.


