8.5 Ordinary Applications described by Section 3 are excluded from
Section 8.4.


============================================================
9. COMPLETE PUBLIC SOURCE REQUIREMENT
============================================================

9.1 Whenever this License requires publication of Source Code, You must
make the source publicly accessible to everyone without charge.

9.2 The source must be hosted in a publicly accessible version-control
repository.

9.3 The repository must include, to the extent reasonably necessary:

(a) all modified Source Code;
(b) all Rawline Source Code required to build the distributed version;
(c) build scripts;
(d) dependency declarations;
(e) configuration files;
(f) compiler and toolchain requirements;
(g) installation instructions;
(h) packaging scripts;
(i) patches;
(j) relevant source-generation tools;
(k) commit history reasonably representing the development of the
    distributed version; and
(l) sufficient information for a competent developer to reproduce the
    distributed binary.

9.4 You may omit passwords, private keys, credentials, private
certificates, access tokens, and unrelated confidential information.

9.5 You may not satisfy this requirement by publishing intentionally
incomplete, non-building, obfuscated, or materially different source.


============================================================
10. USER MODIFICATION AND DEVICE LOCKDOWN
============================================================

10.1 If You distribute Rawline or Modified Rawline as part of a physical
device, appliance, console, workstation, embedded product, or other
hardware product, recipients must be reasonably capable of installing
and running their own compliant modified Rawline builds.

10.2 Where technical restrictions would otherwise prevent modified
versions from running, You must provide a reasonable method of unlocking,
authorizing, signing, or installing modified versions.

10.3 Where reasonably required, this may include:

(a) unlock procedures;
(b) installation tools;
(c) scripts;
(d) documentation;
(e) user-enrollable signing mechanisms; or
(f) equivalent technical means.

10.4 This Section does not require disclosure of private production
signing keys where an alternative user-controlled installation or
signing method can reasonably be provided.


============================================================
11. ATTRIBUTION AND FORK IDENTITY
============================================================

11.1 Copyright, license, and attribution notices must be preserved.

11.2 Public distributions of Rawline or Modified Rawline must include
prominent user-visible attribution substantially equivalent to:

    "Based on Rawline"

and must provide a visible link or reference to the official Rawline
project.

11.3 Appropriate locations include:

(a) an About page;
(b) System Information;
(c) operating-system credits; or
(d) another similarly visible system interface.

11.4 Modified distributions must use a distinct product name and logo.

11.5 Forks may factually state:

    "Based on Rawline"
    "Derived from Rawline"
    "Rawline-compatible"

provided such statements do not imply endorsement.

11.6 Modified distributions may not use "Rawline" as their primary
product name without separate written permission.


