============================================================
13. HOSTED SERVICES AND CLOUD USE
============================================================

13.1 Running Applications, websites, game servers, databases, internal
systems, development environments, or other unrelated services on
Rawline does not constitute a Hosted Rawline Service.

13.2 You may not commercially or publicly provide a Hosted Rawline
Service without separate written authorization from the Licensor.

13.3 Prohibited unauthorized examples include:

(a) "Rawline Cloud";
(b) hosted Rawline virtual machines;
(c) managed Rawline desktops;
(d) public Rawline shell accounts;
(e) commercial Rawline operating-system hosting;
(f) managed Rawline installations sold as a service; and
(g) substantially equivalent offerings.

13.4 If authorization is granted for a Hosted Rawline Service using a
Modified Rawline version, the Complete Corresponding Source of the
version actually running must be published as required by Section 9.


