15. SECURITY RESEARCH
============================================================

15.1 Security research on Rawline is permitted subject to this Section.

15.2 A researcher discovering a previously unknown vulnerability must
make a reasonable good-faith effort to disclose the vulnerability
privately to the Licensor before publishing technical exploitation
details.

15.3 Public disclosure is permitted after the earliest of:

(a) publication of a fix;
(b) written authorization by the Licensor; or
(c) ninety (90) days after a complete private report was received,
    unless the researcher and Licensor mutually agree to extend the
    period.

15.4 This Section does not prohibit ordinary discussion of already
public vulnerabilities.


