32. SHORT VERSION FOR HUMANS
============================================================

This Section is explanatory. If it conflicts with the legal terms above,
the legal terms above control.

You may:

- use Rawline personally;
- study it;
- modify it privately;
- use it inside a company;
- build proprietary software for it;
- sell proprietary Applications that run on it;
- run commercial websites and services on it;
- write proprietary userspace drivers using public driver APIs;
- make non-commercial forks;
- experiment with it;
- use AI tools to help develop it.

You may not, without permission:

- sell Rawline itself;
- sell a Rawline fork;
- rebrand Rawline and turn it into Your commercial OS;
- sell hosted Rawline VMs/desktops/services;
- hide source where this License requires publication;
- lock users out of installing modified Rawline on hardware You ship;
- call a fork "Rawline";
- train or fine-tune an AI model on the Rawline source;
- patent-attack Rawline while continuing to enjoy this License.

If You publicly distribute a modified Rawline:

- keep it non-commercial unless separately authorized;
- publish the complete Source Code;
- publish the build system;
- publish the relevant history;
- make the distributed build reproducible;
- clearly state that it is based on Rawline;
- use Your own name and branding.

The basic rule is:

    Build things ON Rawline: go ahead.

    Learn from and modify Rawline for fun: go ahead.

    Take Rawline itself and make money from my work:
    talk to me first.


